  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "In the adjoining figure, the triangle \\(ABC\\) is a right triangle with \\(\\angle BCA=90^\\circ.\\) Median \\(CM\\) is perpendicular to median \\(BN,\\) and side \\(BC=s.\\) The length of \\(BN\\) is",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(s\\sqrt2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\frac32s\\sqrt2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(2s\\sqrt2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{s\\sqrt5}{2}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{s\\sqrt6}{2}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1982-p21.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Set \\(C=(0,0),\\) \\(B=(0,s),\\) and \\(A=(t,0).\\) Then \\(M=(\\frac{t}{2},\\frac{s}{2})\\) and \\(N=(\\frac{t}{2},0).\\) Perpendicularity gives \\((\\frac{t}{2},\\frac{s}{2})\\cdot(\\frac{t}{2},-s)=0,\\) hence \\(t^2=2s^2.\\) Therefore \\[ \\begin{aligned} BN&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{t}{2})^2+s^2}\\\\ &=\\sqrt{\\frac{s^2}{2}+s^2}\\\\ &=\\frac{s\\sqrt6}{2}. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Place \\(C=(0,0),\\) \\(B=(0,s),\\) and \\(A=(t,0)\\)",
        "Use a dot product for the directions of the two medians"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
